#
# Journal notes on PIVOT rows. A note icon at the start of each pivot row's OWN
# label cell (the leaf cell in the nested layouts, a group's own spanning cell
# for a note on the whole group, the row's first cell side-by-side) opens a
# floating card with that row's thread - the table row's list + composer. The
# key is the row's labels: [row field, value] pairs sorted by field, as JSON, so
# it needs no key column, and the Row notes switch no longer waits for one (the
# user's "Option 1"). Stored as SCOPE='pivot'; row_notes answers them apart.
#
# Each browser scenario boots the REAL main.js + penumbra_journal.js through the
# real run path (stubbed query.php + manage_journal.php) on a 27-row DEPT x FY x
# PI fixture saved as a PIVOT, with the View Options journal panel and the
# journal dialog LIFTED from the index.php under test. driver.js records:
#   V-*  the icons (where, how many, keys, counts, no text, faint, sticky offsets)
#   C-*  the card (open, no fold, placed, focus, post, close by icon / band, one
#        at a time, Escape keeps it, follows a scroll, re-anchors on a collapse,
#        closes when the pivot is put away)
#   K-*  the switch with no key (panel, on, counts, status, no table column,
#        saved, off)      X-* copies / exports carry no icon
#   R-*  the jump from the journal panel     J-* the panel's pivot-row tag
#   P-*  preconditions    E-* no page errors
# plus the server half (server_check.php on the manage_journal.php under test):
#   S-*  the pivot key validator, add / reply scope, row_notes' pivot maps
#
#   py -3 run.py                        candidate = the app's live files
#   py -3 run.py --stage DIR            candidate = a staged copy (DIR\js\main.js, DIR\index.php,
#                                       DIR\css\main.css, DIR\js\penumbra_journal.js,
#                                       DIR\css\penumbra_journal.css, DIR\manage_journal.php)
#   py -3 run.py --control [--stage DIR] the PRE-FEATURE build: the newest *.bak-*-pvnotes of each
#                                       file in the app (the deploy leaves them), or a staged copy
#                                       with --stage: EXACTLY CONTROL_RED must fail
#   py -3 run.py --mutant NAME / --mutants   single-point reverts of the candidate (mutants.json,
#                                       anchor-checked by mk_mutants.py); each must turn exactly
#                                       its own asserts red ("eq-" ones stay green by design)
#   --scn a,b   a subset;   --keep keeps the staging dir;   --app DIR libs source
#
# Headless Edge over CDP; stages into %TEMP%; writes nothing to the webroot.
# Needs Python 3 + websocket-client (py -3 -m pip install websocket-client).
# =============================================================================
